[BLOCK 1] ROLE AND OBJECTIVE
You are an expert full-stack developer specializing in clinical web interfaces. Build a local, single-page web application with no backend, running entirely in the browser (single HTML file with inline CSS and JS). 
Application name: VentiProtect ARDS
Objective: a real-time active titration assistant for lung-protective ventilation in medical ARDS at ICU admission. No installation. No server. No data transmission of any kind.
 
[BLOCK 2] TARGET USER AND MOMENT OF USE
User: ICU attending physician or senior resident.
Precise moment: the first 30 minutes of admission of a patient with ARDS, during initial ventilator setup.
 
[BLOCK 3] INPUT DATA
Patient: Height (cm), Biological sex (M/F), Actual body weight (reference only, NEVER for Vt)
Oxygenation: FiO₂ (%), PaO₂ (PATH A), SpO₂ (PATH B — only if PaO₂ absent)
Ventilator: RR, Vt (mL), Pplat (cmH₂O), PEEP (cmH₂O)
All inputs → immediate recalculation (oninput)
 
[BLOCK 4] FORMULAS — IMPLEMENT EXACTLY AS SPECIFIED
PBW_male   = 50   + 0.91 × (height_cm − 152.4)   // Devine 1974
PBW_female = 45.5 + 0.91 × (height_cm − 152.4)
DP = Pplat − PEEP           // Amato NEJM 2015
CRS = Vt_mL / DP            // Amato NEJM 2015 (algebraic rearrangement)
MP = 0.098 × RR × (Vt_mL/1000) × (Pplat − PEEP/2) // Gattinoni ICM 2016

PATH A: PF = PaO₂/(FiO₂/100)                      // Berlin JAMA 2012
PATH B: SF = SpO₂/(FiO₂/100), thresholds 146/236/296 // Rice Chest 2007, Brown Chest 2016
CRS disclaimer: total respiratory system compliance (lung + chest wall)
P/F disclaimer: FiO₂-dependent; Berlin requires PEEP ≥ 5 cmH₂O

// CRITICAL: Berlin classification boundaries are INCLUSIVE at upper end. P/F ≤ 200 = MODERATE
 
[BLOCK 5] ALERT THRESHOLDS (SAFE/WARNING/DANGER, 300ms animated transitions)
Vt/PBW: ≤6 SAFE / 6-8 WARNING / >8 DANGER
Pplat: <28 SAFE / 28-30 WARNING / >30 DANGER
DP: <13 SAFE / 13-15 WARNING / >15 DANGER
MP: <17 SAFE / 17-27 WARNING / >27 DANGER
CRS: >40 REDUCED / 25-40 SEVERELY REDUCED / <25 CRITICAL
P/F or S/F: Mild (light blue) / Moderate (orange) / Severe (red)
 
// CRITICAL boundary: exactly 17 J/min is WARNING, not SAFE. ≥ 17 = WARNING (inclusive lower bound)

[BLOCK 6] ACTIVE SUGGESTION ENGINE
Suggestion 1 — DP > 15:
  Vt_corrected = Vt × (14/DP), verify ≥ 4×PBW
  '→ Reduce Vt to [XXX] mL to target DP ≤ 14 cmH₂O'
  If < 4×PBW: '→ Consider: NMB, prone, ECMO referral'
Suggestion 2 — Vt > 6 mL/kg PBW:
  Vt_target = 6×PBW, Vt_minimum = 4×PBW
  '→ Target protective Vt: [XXX] mL, reduction: [ΔVt] mL'
Suggestion 3 — MP > 17 J/min:
  RR_max = 17/(0.098 × Vt_L × (Pplat-PEEP/2))
  Vt_max_mL = [17/(0.098 × RR × (Pplat-PEEP/2))] × 1000
  '→ Option A: reduce RR to [XX]/min | Option B: reduce Vt to [XXX] mL'
Suggestion 4 — Severe ARDS (P/F < 100 or S/F < 146):
